ications You must be signed in to change notification settings\nL126:   * cite64†Fork 16.2k L127:   * cite64†Star L128: \nL129:   * cite63†Code L130:   * cite65†Issues 2k L131:   * cite66†Pull requests 619 L132:   * cite67†Actions L133:   * cite68†Projects L134:   * cite69†Wiki L135:   * cite70†Security and quality 13 L136:   * cite71†Insights L137: \nL138: Additional navigation options\nL139: # PO Token Guide\nL140: \nL141: cite72†Jump to bottom L142: \nL143: VXsz edited this page Jul 12, 2026 · cite73†6 revisions L144: \nL145: cite74†Go to YouTube Extractor Wiki L146: # YouTube PO Token Guide\nL147: \nL148: Tip\nL149: \nL150: TL;DR recommended setup: Use a cite75†PO Token Provider plugin to provide the `mweb` client with a cite76†PO Token for GVS requests .\nL151: \nL152: See the notice in the cite74†YouTube Extractor Wiki for more information on the current state of downloading videos from YouTube.\nL153:   * cite77†YouTube PO Token Guide L154:     * cite78†Introduction L155:     * cite76†Cases where a PO Token is required L156:       * cite79†Current PO Token enforcement L157:     * cite75†PO Token Provider Plugins L158:       * cite80†Featured Plugins L159:     * cite81†Other PO Token related tools L160:     * cite82†Technical details L161: ## Introduction\nL162: \nL163: Proof of Origin (PO) Token is a parameter that YouTube requires to be sent with requests from some clients. Without it, requests for the affected clients' format URLs may return HTTP Error 403, or result in your account or IP address being blocked.\nL164: \nL165: A PO Token is generated by an attestation provider on Web, Android and iOS platforms to attest the requests are coming from a genuine client.\nL166: For yt-dlp, you can provide PO Token(s) using the cite83†`po_token` extractor argument , or you can cite75†install a plugin that hooks into the YouTube extractor to handle fetching a PO Token.\nL167: \nL168: For more technical details on these tokens, refer to the cite82†technical details section .\nL169: ## Cases where a PO Token is required\nL170: \nL171: There are currently three cases yt-dlp may require PO Tokens for video downloads, cite79†depending on the client used :\nL172: \nL173:   * GVS: Google Video Server requests (video streaming - https, dash, hls, etc.)\nL174:   * Player: Innertube `player` requests (fetch video format URLs)\nL175:   * Subs: Subtitle requests\nL176: \nL177: The PO Tokens may be generated differently for each of these cases, depending on the client.\nL178: ### Current PO Token enforcement\nL179: \nL180: YouTube is at present rolling out changes to enforce PO Tokens for video playback. Currently, only GVS and Subs require PO Tokens for some clients.\nL181: Client  | PO Token Required For  | Notes\nL182: --- | --- | ---\nL183: `web`  | Subs, GVS  | Only SABR formats available\nL184: `web_safari`  | GVS*  | Same as `web`. *Provides HLS (m3u8) formats which do not require PO Token for GVS at this time.\nL185: `mweb`  | GVS  |\nL186: `tv`  | Not required  | All formats DRM'd if cookies (logged-in or active guest) aren't passed. Only SABR formats available in some cases\nL187: `tv_simply`  | GVS  | Account cookies not supported\nL188: `web_embedded`  | Not required  | Only embeddable videos available\nL189: `web_music`  | GVS  |\nL190: `web_creator`  | GVS  | Requires account cookies\nL191: `android`  | GVS or Player  | Account cookies not supported\nL192: `android_vr`  | Not required  | \"Made for kids\" videos are not available\nL193: `ios`  | GVS or Player  | Account cookies not supported\nL194: For all clients:\nL195: \nL196:   * GVS PO Token is not required for YouTube Premium subscribers\nL197:   * HLS live streams do not require a PO Token (excluding `ios` client)\nL198: \nL199: You can select what client to use with the cite83†`player_client` extractor argument .\nL200: ## PO Token Provider Plugins\nL201: \nL202: Tip\nL203: \nL204: Recommended\nL205: \nL206: Manually extracting PO Tokens is no longer recommended. YouTube now binds PO Tokens to the video ID, so a new token needs to be generated for each video.\nL207: \nL208: It is recommended to use a PO Token Provider plugin to automatically fetch and provide PO Tokens to yt-dlp.\nL209: ### Featured Plugins\nL210: \nL211: Note\nL212: \nL213: These plugins are not affiliated with yt-dlp\nL214: \nL215:   * cite84†bgutil-ytdlp-pot-provider by cite85†Brainicism L216:     * A PO Token Provider which uses cite86†BgUtils to generate PO Tokens. Maintained by a yt-dlp maintainer\nL217:   * cite87†yt-dlp-getpot-wpc by cite88†coletdjnz L218:     * A PO Token Provider which uses YouTube in the browser to generate PO Tokens. Useful as a fallback/alternative if the above fails. Maintained by a yt-dlp core maintainer\nL219: Check out the cite89†yt-dlp-pot-provider GitHub topic for more PO Token Provider plugins.\nL220: \nL221: For developers, refer to the cite90†PO Token Provider developer documentation L222: ## Other PO Token related tools\nL223: \nL224:   * cite86†BgUtils by cite91†LuanRT L225:     * Utility to generate PoTokens and run BotGuard attestation challenges.\nL226:   * cite92†YouTube Trusted Session Generator by cite93†Invidious L227:     * A generator for getting a session that passes all the checks from YouTube side\nL228: ## Technical details\nL229: \nL230: PO Tokens are still an active area of research, and at the same time YouTube is continuously updating the implementation and enforcement. The following information is based on the current understanding of PO Tokens, and is subject to change.\nL231: \nL232: A PO Token is generated by either BotGuard (Web), DroidGuard (Android), iOSGuard (iOS). A PO Token from one platform cannot be used on another (i.e., Web PO Token cannot be used on Android or iOS).\nL233: PO Tokens have a \"content binding\", meaning they are bound to the user session (Visitor ID or account Session ID) or to the video ID. Most PO Tokens (such as for `web` GVS/Player) are bound to the video ID, so a new token is required for each video.\nL234: \nL235: These PO Tokens have a limited lifespan (possibly as short as 12 hours), so they will need to be refreshed periodically. However, some reports suggest that the token may be valid for several months.\nL236: If you are interested, we recommend checking out the cite86†BgUtils project which does a deeper dive into the BotGuard attestation process.\nL237: ## Wiki pages Pages 9\nL238: \nL239: [Input: Find a page or section…]\nL240: \nL241:   * Loading cite69†Home L242: \nL243: ### Uh oh!\nL244: \nL245: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL246: \nL247:   * Loading cite94†EJS L248: \nL249: ### Uh oh!\nL250: \nL251: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL252: \nL253:   * Loading cite95†Extractors L254: \nL255: ### Uh oh!\nL256: \nL257: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL258: \nL259:   * Loading cite96†FAQ L260: \nL261: ### Uh oh!\nL262: \nL263: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL264: \nL265:   * Loading cite97†Forks L266: ### Uh oh!\nL267: \nL268: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL269: \nL270:   * Loading cite98†Installation L271: \nL272: ### Uh oh!\nL273: \nL274: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL275: \nL276:   * Loading cite99†Plugin Development L277: \nL278: ### Uh oh!\nL279: \nL280: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL281: \nL282:   * Loading cite100†Plugins L283: \nL284: ### Uh oh!\nL285: \nL286: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL287: \nL288:   * Loading cite101†PO Token Guide L289: \nL290: ### Uh oh!\nL291: \nL292: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL293: ### Clone this wiki locally\nL294: \nL295: [Input]\nL296: \nL297: You can’t perform that action 