 source is UTF-8 across all platforms.\n\nTo fix this problem, add a magic coding comment at the top of the file, as shown in Example 4-7.\n\nExample 4-7. ola.py: \"Hello, World!\" in Portuguese\n    \n    `# coding: cp1252\n    print('Olá, Mundo!')\n    `\n\nNow that Python 3 source code is no longer limited to ASCII and defaults to the excellent UTF-8 encoding, the best \"fix\" for source code in legacy encodings like 'cp1252' is to convert them to UTF-8 already, and not bother with the coding comments. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nqwen-code/docs/developers/tools/file-system.md at main · QwenLM/qwen-code · GitHub (https://github.com/QwenLM/qwen-code/blob/main/docs/developers/tools/file-system.md)\nciteturn4search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; `utf-8`  | UTF-8 without BOM, no automatic adjustments ... Set it in `.qwen/settings.json` or `~/.qwen/settings.json`: ... On Windows with a non-UTF-8 system code page (e.g.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUmdfied build of npm-run-all · GitHub (https://gist.github.com/umdfied/8c9cae20baec6c85fbff2c6cd3f1a8c2)\nciteturn4search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: last week;  | // Attempts to complete a partial non-UTF-8 character using bytes from a Buffer ...  | // @TODO There should be a utf8-strict encoding that rejects invalid UTF-8 code ...  | notHost.unshift(bit[2]); ...  | this.warn(\"nonStringDependency\", d, JSON.stringify(r))\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a046ba-a53b-70c0-a89e-a374ccd6f3ba","create_time":1787893224.973498}}}
